{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787060613,"nonce":"Id94LF7e33iTIaVnBhBt4dSVgHw=","title":"`notifications.subject_kind` and `channel_threads.subject_kind` admit only `alert_group`, so an ack cannot say what it is about","message":"**What is wrong.** Both tables model a subject as a `(kind, id)` pair and then constrain the kind to a\nsingle value. So every notification claims the alert group as its subject even when the fact it carries is\nabout one case — an acknowledgement is a receipt against a case, and the row says it is about the group of\nforty. The same constraint on `channel_threads` welds thread identity to the alert grouping, so a\nconversation can only ever be keyed by a group, whatever the policy would prefer.\n\n**The demonstration.** `db/migrations/00011_notification.sql:170` — `threads_subjkind_ck CHECK (subject_kind\nIN ('alert_group'))` — and the equivalent `notifications_subjkind_ck`. `notifications` already carries\n`alert_id` and `case_id` alongside `group_id`, and `notifications.alert_id`'s comment\n(`00011_notification.sql:248`) already says it is \"MANDATORY for acked, unacked, refired and rule_changed\",\nso the schema already knows the subject varies. Only the CHECK pretends otherwise.\n\n**Why it matters.** The subject is what a notification is ABOUT; the group is where it is DELIVERED. Fusing\nthem means an ack cannot be addressed, a digest cannot be threaded, and any future conversation key is\nblocked by a one-line constraint rather than by a design. It also makes `subject_id` unusable as a join key,\nbecause its meaning is fixed rather than declared.\n\n**Where.** `db/migrations/00011_notification.sql:150-175,202-256` · `internal/notification/domain/reason.go:18-66`\n(the 18 reasons to map) · `internal/channels/domain/ports.go:135-146` (the render modes) ·\n`internal/notification/domain/mode.go` · `docs/design/SPEC.md` §D.8, §H.6.\n\n**Scope.** medium\n\n**Done when.**\n1. Both CHECKs admit `alert | case | alert_group`, and `subject_id` agrees with the matching id column,\n   enforced by a CHECK rather than by convention.\n2. Every reason is assigned a subject, and a test asserts the mapping is total — a nineteenth reason cannot\n   be added without deciding what it is about. The allocation decides it: `acked`/`unacked` are case-subject\n   because ack is a case verb; `snoozed`/`unsnoozed`/`suppressed`/`unsuppressed` are alert-subject because\n   those are alert axes; `new_alerts`/`some_resolved`/`all_resolved` are group-subject.\n3. `group_id` stays NOT NULL and is re-commented as the DELIVERY TARGET, not the subject. Threading is\n   unchanged: forty alerts still produce one thread.\n4. `UNIQUE (channel_id, subject_kind, subject_id)` continues to mean exactly one conversation per subject.\n5. `enriched` and `rule_changed` are assigned deliberately and the reasoning recorded — the rule snapshot is\n   a per-firing fact, which argues case, but the drift being reported is about the alert's rule.","files":null}]}